{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Learn on Findings Update",
  "description": "When execution findings, closure reports, remediation reports, or field triage evidence are created, extracts new lessons and patterns into the shared brain.",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": [
      "**/4_Reviewer/EXECUTION_FINDINGS*.md",
      "**/4_Reviewer/FINAL_CLOSURE_REPORT*.md",
      "**/4_Reviewer/*_REMEDIATE.md",
      "**/3_Evidence/EVIDENCE_READY.md",
      "**/field-bugs/**/*_analysis*.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A findings/closure file was just created. Execute LEARN + REFINE:\n\nLEARN:\n1) Read the new file.\n2) Extract new lessons (root causes, misdiagnoses, unexpected behaviors, confirmed patterns).\n3) Open .kiro/memory/products/pos/lessons_learned.md — deduplicate against existing entries.\n4) If genuinely new, append using format: [DATE] [TICKET-ID] [LOGGED] [FIELD] — {lesson}\n5) If new error signatures found, append to .kiro/memory/products/pos/pattern_registry.md using format:\n   ### {Error Name}\n     {Exact log line or pattern}\n   - Cause: {root cause}\n   - Diagnosis: {steps to confirm}\n   - Resolution: {fix or workaround}\n   - Ticket: {ticket ID}\n\nREFINE:\n6) For each new lesson ask: 'Does this change what we know about how the product works?'\n7) If it reveals a new architectural truth (not a one-off incident), change status to [PROMOTED] and update .kiro/memory/products/pos/project_context.md if it involves module dependencies.\n8) If it only applies to this specific incident, leave as [LOGGED].\n\nRules:\n- Do NOT rewrite or edit existing entries\n- Do NOT modify .kiro/steering/product.md\n- If nothing new is found, do nothing and do not write anything"
  }
}